editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:129:- **The cold months (131st–264th)** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] (≈14,000). The first week of ice. The pricing scene at the inn. The cold-term board [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. The fence trip. The river becoming a road. Hesk and Vell's letters gone west on the last ferry, with the answers pending. Karis's back room. The long dark. The thaw. Pike in his room. The source's log entries become scenes, and the log stays as punctuation between them.
