    56	
    57	"He says five months," said Brom. "First snow to first boat. He's seen a good many, and he's been out by a week and never by two."
    58	
    59	They were in the store behind the chimney at noon, the five of them, which was two more than it had been built to hold. Karis had the table. Lira sat on a meal-sack with the great boot stuck out before her, and Brom filled the doorway, since there was nowhere else that he would go. Seln had the sill of the one small window, and had contrived to take up no room on it.
