    61	In the west each of them had been a line in a registry: an Ember of the third rank in Iron, and a Wind of the first; an Iron Skin who had stopped at Copper and said so without shame; and a Shadow, Bronze, whom fifteen years of service had taught to be overlooked. Nobody out here had asked any of them for a tier since the ninth day. The board at the foot of the meadow priced the job and never the person. By its reckoning the five of them stood eleventh among the crews on a sheet of sailcloth, which was all the rank that this country kept.
