   227	"You put your hands up," said Teague afterward, without any unkindness. "It's a good way to choose a road. It's no way to cross a yard."
   228	
   229	Cael entered that as he would have entered a touch taken. *He is better at this than I am. The cloth has said so since we first read it, and the cloth is right.*
   230	
   231	---
   232	
   233	The river was a river again at the middle on the two hundred and thirtieth day.
   234	
   235	It had been coming for a week. The ferryman had pulled his green on the two hundred and twenty-fourth, bough by bough, and stood them against his rope-house. The road-ice went grey, and then it went dull, and a carter who tried it against advice put a wheel through at the landing's foot and was laughed at. By the two hundred and thirtieth morning there was a lane of black water down the channel, as wide as the scow was long, with the shelves standing white on either hand and cakes of ice turning in the current.
