   281	The carter came over the saddle the next morning with his breeches wet to the thigh, and said that the road was open if a person did not mind the ford.
   282	
   283	Lira had been ready since before it was light. The bow was on her back, with its one bolt, and the sling was knotted high at her collar-bone as a healer had left it at a fork. She had not spoken of that arm since a strip of bark was read out at a hearth, and she did not speak of it now. She went up the saddle road first, on the whole of her foot, and the rest of them followed her.

